  "schema_version": 1,
  "description": "The walkable town (WP16 slice). Each room is 11 tiles wide; map rows are 11 characters, one per 16 px tile, looked up in legend. Coordinates are [x, y] in tiles from the top-left. exits: walking onto one of its tiles moves to room 'to' at spawn 'arrive' (kind door fades, kind edge slides in 'dir'). props and npcs are things to tap or drop items on; their id is the target the chain data names. rect_px [x, y, w, h] in room pixels replaces at/size for hotspots inside a big prop. stand is where the player walks to first (default: the nearest walkable tile beside it). say lists story piece ids shown in turn when no chain interaction applies; open names a menu or close-up. sound is the quiet ambient loop (an id in data/sfx.json); ambient adds motion: steam, gulls, sparkle, bubbles.",
